        "created_at": "2012-11-12T19:12:37.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>According to the EE rules,</p><p>&nbsp; Conflict Resolution,</p><p>&nbsp; \"In all situations, card effects that happen simultaneously occur in the order in which the cards entered play.\"</p><p>According to Spiff's rules clarification,</p><p>&nbsp; Skipping Your Turn,</p><p>&nbsp; \"If you have other things that should happen during your start-of-turn phase, you get to decide the order in which they happen, so you could decide to let any other start-of-turn effects happen first, then skip the rest of your turn\"</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp;Ties, Timing and Teh Order Abilities Take Place,</p><p>&nbsp; \"1) Abilities take place In the order their cards were played, ...\"</p><p>===</p><p>Is there a contradiction between the \"Skipping your turn\" and \"Ties, Timing etc.\"? From reading the rules as is, the effect of the Start of Phase is played strictly on the Card into play order; the players do not get a choice on resolving the Start of Phase orders. Am I missing something?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:36:40.834Z",
