        "id": 44188,
        "name": "Ameena",
        "username": "Ameena",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-11-12T23:38:52.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I don't put my cards in sequence, but in an order that makes more sense to look at (so \"start of turn\" things are to the left, whereas damage-power stuff will be to the right). Ra's staff I always put on the far left of my line-up, for example, and the Adept's instruments are always left, followed by Harmonies, then Melodies, then Rhythms. Villain and Environment cards I always keep in play order, however, and \"activate\" in play order when their various actions need to be played out.</p>",
        "post_number": 6,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:17:46.042Z",
