        "raw": "<p>Yep, I had it wrong in a previous version of my doc, but the one that&#39;s currently available has the corrected version.&nbsp; Sorry for the confusion.</p><p>My current wording:</p><blockquote><p>But what about your start-of-turn phase? in most cases, cards will say &ldquo;at the start of your turn, you may skip the rest of your turn to do xyz&rdquo;. because cards are activated in a phase in the order they were played, if you have other cards with start-of-turn effects which were in play before the card which is causing you to skip the rest of your turn, those start-of-turn effects will happen first, then you&rsquo;ll skip everything else.</p></blockquote><p>As always, if anyone sees that I&#39;ve got the wrong info, please be sure to let me know so I can correct it.</p>",
